<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (Commercial password-auditing tools and the classic CUPP \(Common User Passwords Profiler\) already demonstrate this idea. For a student laboratory, however, a small, fully understandable implementation that also includes an offline dictionary-attack demonstration against self-generated sample hashes is more educational. The problem addressed here is therefore to design and implement a readable Python toolkit that \(1\) builds a custom wordlist from a personal profile using realistic mangling rules and \(2\) measures its effectiveness against sample hashes in a completely isolated, ethical setting.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
