>>
endobj
248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 90 0 R
/T (A dictionary \(or wordlist\) attack hashes each candidate string from a prepared list and compares the result with a stored password hash. Because the search space is limited to the list, the attack is far faster than pure brute-force when the true password is among the candidates. Modern tools \(hashcat, John the Ripper\) combine large base dictionaries with rule-based mangling engines that apply thousands of transformations on the fly. The effectiveness of any dictionary attack therefore depends on how well the candidate list matches the password-creation habits of the target population.)
/E (A dictionary \(or wordlist\) attack hashes each candidate string from a prepared list and compares the result with a stored password hash. Because the search space is limited to the list, the attack is far faster than pure brute-force when the true password is among the candidates. Modern tools \(hashcat, John the Ripper\) combine large base dictionaries with rule-based mangling engines that apply thousands of transformations on the fly. The effectiveness of any dictionary attack therefore depends on how well the candidate list matches the password-creation habits of the target population.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
