499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (A complete, self-contained CUPP-style custom wordlist generator with realistic mangling rules was implemented in pure Python and paired with an offline dictionary-attack demonstration module. The tool accepts either an interactive questionnaire or a JSON profile, extracts personal tokens, applies case, leetspeak, numeric, date and special-character transformations, and writes a size-capped candidate list. Against self-generated sample hashes derived from the same profile the basic wordlist achieved a 100 % recovery rate for the planted weak passwords, while passwords outside the profile remained uncracked.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
500 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (All objectives listed in Section 1.2 were met. The project also satisfies the ethical constraints of the Cyber Security Lab: only invented data, only local execution, and a clear declaration that the techniques must never be used against systems or accounts without explicit authorisation. The work illustrates both the power of targeted wordlists and the corresponding defensive lesson that personal information should never be the foundation of a password.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
