1201 0 obj
<<
/Title (A dictionary \(or wordlist\) attack hashes each candidate string from a prepared list and compares the result with a stored password hash. Because the search space is limited to the list, the attack is far faster than pure brute-force when the true password is among the candidates. Modern tools \(hashcat, John the Ripper\) combine large base dictionaries with rule-based mangling engines that apply thousands of transformations on the fly. The effectiveness of any dictionary attack therefore depends on how well the candidate list matches the password-creation habits of the target population.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1190 0 R
>>
endobj
